(1189896, 147286, 31307, '<td valign="top">I knew that submitting a photo like this was risky in that not many people would get it.  I figured it was worth it.  I wear my indivuality like a badge of honor--even to my own detriment.  For those who aren''t very computer hardware knowledgable, there are two chipsets on a motherboard either side of the PCI bus known as bridges.  The one above the PCI bus is the north bridge and the one below, as you can guess, is called the south bridge.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-03-21 19:40:10.</i></td>', 'I knew that submitting a photo like this was risky in that not many people would get it.  I figured it was worth it.  I wear my indivuality like a badge of honor--even to my own detriment.  For those who aren''t very computer hardware knowledgable, there are two chipsets on a motherboard either side of the PCI bus known as bridges.  The one above the PCI bus is the north bridge and the one below, as you can guess, is called the south bridge.', '2005-02-23 02:02:31.000000', '2005-03-21 19:40:10.000000', 0),
(1189898, 146849, 31637, '<td valign="top">the perspective on this is amazing. I originally gave you a 6. It is a very above average composition. you seem to have an eye for photography, and this photo is proof of that. I like the black and white, and what a great vantage point !! good job</td>', 'the perspective on this is amazing. I originally gave you a 6. It is a very above average composition. you seem to have an eye for photography, and this photo is proof of that. I like the black and white, and what a great vantage point !! good job', '2005-02-23 02:02:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(1189899, 146912, 31990, '<td valign="top">Well, 47 out of 418 is not so bad for my first entry <br/>I should not be happy though ! :)<br/>To: <b>ali626</b>, <b>cosmic</b>, <b>scuds</b>, <b>AJFI</b>, <b>Toniann220</b>, <b>ltsimring</b>, <b>Fleximus</b>, <b>rigrider</b>, <b>AJAger</b>, <b>magus_rex</b> : <br/> - Thank you very much for your comments.<br/>To: <b>RulerZigzag</b> - I made over 30 shots and I have some of them much closer to the bridge. Not bad at all but I didn''t want to lose the boats (Chinese restaurants on the water). I thought the picture is too simple. Thank you for your comment.<br/>To: <b>nikolayi</b> - I used the standard 24-85 Canon lenses. Thank you for your comment! I would love to have a 14 mm but too expensive!<br/>To <b>Azrifel</b>: I added as much sharpness as I could without destroying the quality. Especially on the water where the bridge is reflected. <br/>Compression kills. :( <br/>Thank you for your comment!<br/>---<br/>Though I am really new here I think it is a site where I can learn a lot. I will definitely try harder for the next challenges. <br/>A good day to everyone.<br/>Mircea</td>', 'Well, 47 out of 418 is not so bad for my first entry I should not be happy though ! :)To: ali626, cosmic, scuds, AJFI, Toniann220, ltsimring, Fleximus, rigrider, AJAger, magus_rex :  - Thank you very much for your comments.To: RulerZigzag - I made over 30 shots and I have some of them much closer to the bridge. Not bad at all but I didn''t want to lose the boats (Chinese restaurants on the water). I thought the picture is too simple. Thank you for your comment.To: nikolayi - I used the standard 24-85 Canon lenses. Thank you for your comment! I would love to have a 14 mm but too expensive!To Azrifel: I added as much sharpness as I could without destroying the quality. Especially on the water where the bridge is reflected. Compression kills. :( Thank you for your comment!---Though I am really new here I think it is a site where I can learn a lot. I will definitely try harder for the next challenges. A good day to everyone.Mircea', '2005-02-23 02:02:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(1189900, 147452, 30835, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all the helpful comments.  The most disappointing thing for me was trying to get the symmetry right.  It was difficult to achieve due to the time I had to take the shot in (without getting knocked down by trucks!!).  Also the basic editing doesn''t allow me to straighten it in Photoshop, so it was left as taken. I went for the most graphic look, high contrast, I thought the white sky quite effective, I was pleased to see so many people apreciated this.  I don''t agree with Kathy about requiring an angle, that wasn''t the point with this image, ''space'' is created in other ways here.</td>', 'Thanks for all the helpful comments.  The most disappointing thing for me was trying to get the symmetry right.  It was difficult to achieve due to the time I had to take the shot in (without getting knocked down by trucks!!).  Also the basic editing doesn''t allow me to straighten it in Photoshop, so it was left as taken. I went for the most graphic look, high contrast, I thought the white sky quite effective, I was pleased to see so many people apreciated this.  I don''t agree with Kathy about requiring an angle, that wasn''t the point with this image, ''space'' is created in other ways here.', '2005-02-23 02:03:03.000000', NULL, 0),
