(1190460, 147345, 25331, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by mitähä:</b></div><hr/><i> Good picture.<br/>But You need a sharper lens.<br/> <br/>A 7. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>I used a 10-22 f/3.5-4.5  The lens itself is not so bad. But at 10mm, the details tend to become very small. I agree that I could have done a USM. I took the same using the 24-70L, the pic is different and yes, sharper..<br/><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-02-23 10:23:55.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by mitähä: Good picture.But You need a sharper lens. A 7.  I used a 10-22 f/3.5-4.5  The lens itself is not so bad. But at 10mm, the details tend to become very small. I agree that I could have done a USM. I took the same using the 24-70L, the pic is different and yes, sharper..', '2005-02-23 10:13:18.000000', '2005-02-23 10:23:55.000000', 0),
(1190463, 145323, 31738, '<td valign="top">Hey Vince, you made 17th place, congratulations, you did very well. Your photo has alot of potential, I believe it should of scored higher than it did but still, good work. I seen your outakes too, Outake2 is awesome, I first noticed it on your web site. Well, good going Vince, take care.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-02-23 10:20:38.</i></td>', 'Hey Vince, you made 17th place, congratulations, you did very well. Your photo has alot of potential, I believe it should of scored higher than it did but still, good work. I seen your outakes too, Outake2 is awesome, I first noticed it on your web site. Well, good going Vince, take care.', '2005-02-23 10:13:46.000000', '2005-02-23 10:20:38.000000', 0),
(1190467, 147345, 25331, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by davidx76:</b></div><hr/><i> I really like this shot, esp keeping some detail in the duck sky.  But the bridge looks like a bit of an after-thought? </i></td></tr></table> <br/>I used a polarizing filter to keep the details in the sky.</td>', 'Originally posted by davidx76: I really like this shot, esp keeping some detail in the duck sky.  But the bridge looks like a bit of an after-thought?  I used a polarizing filter to keep the details in the sky.', '2005-02-23 10:16:29.000000', NULL, 0),
