(1190702, 147553, 31738, '<td valign="top">Ant, Congratulations on your first ribbon, may there be many many more.<br/>I don''t understand why you got so many one''s isn''t that kind of strange?<br/>Good job brother lol<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-02-23 12:34:22.</i></td>', 'Ant, Congratulations on your first ribbon, may there be many many more.I don''t understand why you got so many one''s isn''t that kind of strange?Good job brother lol', '2005-02-23 12:30:42.000000', '2005-02-23 12:34:22.000000', 0),
(1190727, 145672, 5792, '<td valign="top">With all due respect to the wonderful pictures that finished with higher scores, I still think yours is the class of the field and a cut above the rest. It is also better than your own two previous bridge pictures that scored higher. If given the chance this great bridge image will take on a life of its own far beyond this challenge.</td>', 'With all due respect to the wonderful pictures that finished with higher scores, I still think yours is the class of the field and a cut above the rest. It is also better than your own two previous bridge pictures that scored higher. If given the chance this great bridge image will take on a life of its own far beyond this challenge.', '2005-02-23 12:39:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(1190765, 145383, 34093, '<td valign="top">A poorly lit picture of a bridge doesn''t "do it for me".</td>', 'A poorly lit picture of a bridge doesn''t "do it for me".', '2005-02-23 12:51:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(1190778, 147604, 16230, '<td valign="top">Thanks to everybody that took the time to comment. They are much appreciated.<br/> <br/>I just want to point out that this photo is not B&amp;W. Because of the dense fog there was very little color in the original RAW image. I turned down the brightness a little, and increased the contrast. The bridge is actually a grayish green color.</td>', 'Thanks to everybody that took the time to comment. They are much appreciated. I just want to point out that this photo is not B&W. Because of the dense fog there was very little color in the original RAW image. I turned down the brightness a little, and increased the contrast. The bridge is actually a grayish green color.', '2005-02-23 12:56:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(1190893, 147015, 30861, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by nards656:</b></div><hr/><i> Congratulations on yet another excellent photo, Brad.  WHAT!  You left home without a tripod???? :) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>That would be Chuey''s, right? Now there''s an institution for ya...<br/> <br/>Robt.</td>', 'Originally posted by nards656: Congratulations on yet another excellent photo, Brad.  WHAT!  You left home without a tripod???? :)   That would be Chuey''s, right? Now there''s an institution for ya... Robt.', '2005-02-23 13:37:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(1190971, 147015, 18870, '<td valign="top">WELL DONE!  one of the best shots of the Coronado Bridge that I have ever seen.</td>', 'WELL DONE!  one of the best shots of the Coronado Bridge that I have ever seen.', '2005-02-23 14:11:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(1190976, 145993, 33725, '<td valign="top">I like everything about it except the shallow depth of field.  If more had been in focus, I would have scored it higher.</td>', 'I like everything about it except the shallow depth of field.  If more had been in focus, I would have scored it higher.', '2005-02-23 14:13:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(1190984, 147451, 21124, '<td valign="top">Original picture:<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=149753" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/21124/thumb/149753.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/21124/thumb/149753.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/21124/thumb/149753.jpg"/></a></td>', 'Original picture:', '2005-02-23 14:16:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(1191044, 147015, 33435, '<td valign="top">Brad, its time to quit your day job!  Buy that camera you really want, and go for it.  I hope you distribute your photography, or at least show your work in galleries.  I''m new to this whole digital photography thing, but my girlfriend is a highly recognized and accomplished photographer in Philly.  I regularly go to the art galleries, and I see the work that people are doing in a city that is well regarded for being cultured and artistically educated.  Your work blows them all away.  Seriously, by leaps and bounds.   I mean it in a factual way, and not just as my opinion.  Excellent photo, and congratulations on another ribbon!</td>', 'Brad, its time to quit your day job!  Buy that camera you really want, and go for it.  I hope you distribute your photography, or at least show your work in galleries.  I''m new to this whole digital photography thing, but my girlfriend is a highly recognized and accomplished photographer in Philly.  I regularly go to the art galleries, and I see the work that people are doing in a city that is well regarded for being cultured and artistically educated.  Your work blows them all away.  Seriously, by leaps and bounds.   I mean it in a factual way, and not just as my opinion.  Excellent photo, and congratulations on another ribbon!', '2005-02-23 14:38:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(1191097, 147057, 32754, '<td valign="top">Thank you everyone who gave me 5 and above; the others, I would like to tell you: I am trying hard to improve!</td>', 'Thank you everyone who gave me 5 and above; the others, I would like to tell you: I am trying hard to improve!', '2005-02-23 14:57:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(1191123, 146231, 9149, '<td valign="top">Nice concrete texture. Great shot.</td>', 'Nice concrete texture. Great shot.', '2005-02-23 15:05:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(1191128, 147178, 34037, '<td valign="top">I was hoping you would win; its my favorite &amp; absolutely beautiful.</td>', 'I was hoping you would win; its my favorite & absolutely beautiful.', '2005-02-23 15:09:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(1191150, 147536, 27845, '<td valign="top">I agree with dragonlady, this picture should definately have been among the top pictures. I really like it.</td>', 'I agree with dragonlady, this picture should definately have been among the top pictures. I really like it.', '2005-02-23 15:24:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(1191160, 147553, 25232, '<td valign="top">Told you you had it in you. Stay away from entering those setup indoor shots (for now, but keep practicing) and do what it is you do best. Your bridges and cityscapes are awesome.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-02-23 15:27:25.</i></td>', 'Told you you had it in you. Stay away from entering those setup indoor shots (for now, but keep practicing) and do what it is you do best. Your bridges and cityscapes are awesome.', '2005-02-23 15:25:46.000000', '2005-02-23 15:27:25.000000', 0),
(1191163, 147553, 6349, '<td valign="top">Congrats on your first ribbon.  Proud to have called this one.</td>', 'Congrats on your first ribbon.  Proud to have called this one.', '2005-02-23 15:26:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(1191172, 147442, 27845, '<td valign="top">Cool picture, and a great story how it was made. You are one lucky chap. Congratulations.</td>', 'Cool picture, and a great story how it was made. You are one lucky chap. Congratulations.', '2005-02-23 15:33:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(1191219, 147402, 33114, '<td valign="top">83 out of 418 ! Not bad at all. Congratulations.</td>', '83 out of 418 ! Not bad at all. Congratulations.', '2005-02-23 16:00:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(1191223, 147178, 18868, '<td valign="top">I think this is the first image I''ve ever seen that received no "zero" votes.  Well done.</td>', 'I think this is the first image I''ve ever seen that received no "zero" votes.  Well done.', '2005-02-23 16:02:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(1191229, 147015, 19708, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by phreakon:</b></div><hr/><i> Brad, its time to quit your day job!  Buy that camera you really want, and go for it.  I hope you distribute your photography, or at least show your work in galleries.  I''m new to this whole digital photography thing, but my girlfriend is a highly recognized and accomplished photographer in Philly.  I regularly go to the art galleries, and I see the work that people are doing in a city that is well regarded for being cultured and artistically educated.  Your work blows them all away.  Seriously, by leaps and bounds.   I mean it in a factual way, and not just as my opinion.  Excellent photo, and congratulations on another ribbon! </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Mike,<br/> <br/>This is perhaps the highest compliment I have ever received, and thank you from the bottom of my heart. As of now, I have not displayed anything anywhere and only share my images here and at another site. It''s on my list of things to do when I get serious about this hobby.<br/> <br/>Again, Thank You.<br/>Your kind words mean more than any ribbon ever did.</td>', 'Originally posted by phreakon: Brad, its time to quit your day job!  Buy that camera you really want, and go for it.  I hope you distribute your photography, or at least show your work in galleries.  I''m new to this whole digital photography thing, but my girlfriend is a highly recognized and accomplished photographer in Philly.  I regularly go to the art galleries, and I see the work that people are doing in a city that is well regarded for being cultured and artistically educated.  Your work blows them all away.  Seriously, by leaps and bounds.   I mean it in a factual way, and not just as my opinion.  Excellent photo, and congratulations on another ribbon!  Mike, This is perhaps the highest compliment I have ever received, and thank you from the bottom of my heart. As of now, I have not displayed anything anywhere and only share my images here and at another site. It''s on my list of things to do when I get serious about this hobby. Again, Thank You.Your kind words mean more than any ribbon ever did.', '2005-02-23 16:05:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(1191240, 147553, 20066, '<td valign="top">Congrats on yor first ribbon but those 10 "one" voters make me sad!</td>', 'Congrats on yor first ribbon but those 10 "one" voters make me sad!', '2005-02-23 16:11:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(1191251, 145672, 12962, '<td valign="top">3 ones and twos?  They''ve got to be kidding.  I agree with stdavidson.  This is one of those photographs makes you stop and wish that you shot it.  Or dream of taking it, at least.  Congrats on your top ten finish though.</td>', '3 ones and twos?  They''ve got to be kidding.  I agree with stdavidson.  This is one of those photographs makes you stop and wish that you shot it.  Or dream of taking it, at least.  Congrats on your top ten finish though.', '2005-02-23 16:25:22.000000', NULL, 0);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(1191296, 147215, 31637, '<td valign="top">a great capture. All the different people and races, and the great DOF. It is a photo that deserves more than what it recieved but in these bridge challenges, the non physical structures didnt fare to well. This shot belongs in a newspaper or magazine.</td>', 'a great capture. All the different people and races, and the great DOF. It is a photo that deserves more than what it recieved but in these bridge challenges, the non physical structures didnt fare to well. This shot belongs in a newspaper or magazine.', '2005-02-23 16:47:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(1191307, 146862, 3461, '<td valign="top">Wow. Thank you all for your wonderful comments. Even though I didn''t score that highly I feel I made a good image based on your positive reactions.</td>', 'Wow. Thank you all for your wonderful comments. Even though I didn''t score that highly I feel I made a good image based on your positive reactions.', '2005-02-23 16:49:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(1191357, 147553, 30222, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by eirasi:</b></div><hr/><i> Congrats on yor first ribbon but those 10 "one" voters make me sad! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Ruler when u were discussing in a thread the high votes that came in<br/>on ur beautiful shot,  u posted another picture wich probable revealed a bit emphatic what image u sent in for this challenge<br/>so i think the 1-voters did this because they found this move very undone <br/>this is the only reason i can think of regarding the one-voters<br/>pathetic but true<br/>soo maybe for the next time this consideration might be helpfull to u<br/>BOL</td>', 'Originally posted by eirasi: Congrats on yor first ribbon but those 10 "one" voters make me sad!   Ruler when u were discussing in a thread the high votes that came inon ur beautiful shot,  u posted another picture wich probable revealed a bit emphatic what image u sent in for this challengeso i think the 1-voters did this because they found this move very undone this is the only reason i can think of regarding the one-voterspathetic but truesoo maybe for the next time this consideration might be helpfull to uBOL', '2005-02-23 17:15:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(1191376, 146449, 1031, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all the comments, although I assure you that obscuring her head was distinctly on purpose : )<br/>See this <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/forum.php?action=post&amp;FORUM_THREAD_ID=177269" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">thread on Bridge photos</a> for more details.</td>', 'Thanks for all the comments, although I assure you that obscuring her head was distinctly on purpose : )See this thread on Bridge photos for more details.', '2005-02-23 17:23:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(1191425, 147042, 33284, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by utro:</b></div><hr/><i> Gorgeous.  There seem to be two bridges in this photo, the sandbridge across the reflection, and the arc of the reflection itself could symbolize a bridging of earth and sky. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thank you.  Glad you were able to see the "bridge(s)".  You saw another one that I did not see, the bridging of earth and sky.<br/> <br/>Mike</td>', 'Originally posted by utro: Gorgeous.  There seem to be two bridges in this photo, the sandbridge across the reflection, and the arc of the reflection itself could symbolize a bridging of earth and sky.   Thank you.  Glad you were able to see the "bridge(s)".  You saw another one that I did not see, the bridging of earth and sky. Mike', '2005-02-23 17:43:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(1191433, 147042, 33284, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Kylie:</b></div><hr/><i> Simply stunning light and beauty. Great eye to see thsi bridge!! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thank you!!  Not all bridges are man made or so literal.<br/> <br/>Mike</td>', 'Originally posted by Kylie: Simply stunning light and beauty. Great eye to see thsi bridge!!   Thank you!!  Not all bridges are man made or so literal. Mike', '2005-02-23 17:46:51.000000', NULL, 0),
