(1199605, 147551, 33732, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by CBalck:</b></div><hr/><i> The bridge is obstructed by all the trees, but otherwise this is a decent shot. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>This was a hard photo.  Walking out on a bridge to get the photo.  The trees were thick at this angle where I could get most of the train bridge.  The limb at the upper right was left this time.  The massive old bridge was the idea.  No train on it for a while.  pop</td>', 'Originally posted by CBalck: The bridge is obstructed by all the trees, but otherwise this is a decent shot.   This was a hard photo.  Walking out on a bridge to get the photo.  The trees were thick at this angle where I could get most of the train bridge.  The limb at the upper right was left this time.  The massive old bridge was the idea.  No train on it for a while.  pop', '2005-02-28 18:15:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(1199608, 147551, 33732, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by thatannemarie:</b></div><hr/><i> very engrossing composition. i like this a lot. but what is that in the upper right corner? seems out of place. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Left the tree limb in the shot.  Thanks</td>', 'Originally posted by thatannemarie: very engrossing composition. i like this a lot. but what is that in the upper right corner? seems out of place.   Left the tree limb in the shot.  Thanks', '2005-02-28 18:16:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(1199612, 147551, 33732, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by antimethod:</b></div><hr/><i> really cool shot... the color and the structure emerging from a tangle is delicious. if only it were an advanced challenge to handle the top right corner. if you had cropped it a bit on the top for this challenge, however, i bet you could have pulled off a few more points. first impression is great though. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks.  That tree limb really got the attention.  Better next time.<br/></td>', 'Originally posted by antimethod: really cool shot... the color and the structure emerging from a tangle is delicious. if only it were an advanced challenge to handle the top right corner. if you had cropped it a bit on the top for this challenge, however, i bet you could have pulled off a few more points. first impression is great though.   Thanks.  That tree limb really got the attention.  Better next time.', '2005-02-28 18:18:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(1199614, 147551, 33732, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by aronya1:</b></div><hr/><i> Too dark for my taste.  Maybe better in B&amp;W?  Tighter crop?  I''m sure you''ll get complaints about the dark triangle in the top right. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>That tree limb got the comments up in the corner.  Crop next time.<br/> <br/></td>', 'Originally posted by aronya1: Too dark for my taste.  Maybe better in B&W?  Tighter crop?  I''m sure you''ll get complaints about the dark triangle in the top right.   That tree limb got the comments up in the corner.  Crop next time. ', '2005-02-28 18:19:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(1199624, 147551, 33732, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by ltsimring:</b></div><hr/><i> I guess the timing of the shot is not good - it is almost invisible agains the dark background </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>12 hours later would have been different.  This is a hard shot and I wanted blue sky.  The sun angle and the distractions taking the shot from the other side made this a hard subject to capture from this side.<br/> <br/>Thanks<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-02-28 18:27:26.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by ltsimring: I guess the timing of the shot is not good - it is almost invisible agains the dark background   12 hours later would have been different.  This is a hard shot and I wanted blue sky.  The sun angle and the distractions taking the shot from the other side made this a hard subject to capture from this side. Thanks', '2005-02-28 18:22:02.000000', '2005-02-28 18:27:26.000000', 0),
(1199630, 147551, 33732, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by EaThis:</b></div><hr/><i> bad exposure </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>See the green water of the river?  This high bridge and close position is hard to combine.  The south sun keep you from seeing the rust on the bridge.<br/> <br/>Thanks</td>', 'Originally posted by EaThis: bad exposure   See the green water of the river?  This high bridge and close position is hard to combine.  The south sun keep you from seeing the rust on the bridge. Thanks', '2005-02-28 18:24:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(1199633, 147551, 33732, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by ltsimring:</b></div><hr/><i> I guess the timing of the shot is not good - it is almost invisible agains the dark background </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>A tree limb was in the upper corner.  Got the attention.  I wanted the whole photo trees and all but that was one too many.<br/> <br/>Thanks</td>', 'Originally posted by ltsimring: I guess the timing of the shot is not good - it is almost invisible agains the dark background   A tree limb was in the upper corner.  Got the attention.  I wanted the whole photo trees and all but that was one too many. Thanks', '2005-02-28 18:25:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(1199644, 147551, 33732, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by EaThis:</b></div><hr/><i> bad exposure </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I can''t disagree.  First entry.  Did you have an idea for me on this to keep the sky blue while getting lighter on the trees, etc?<br/> <br/></td>', 'Originally posted by EaThis: bad exposure   I can''t disagree.  First entry.  Did you have an idea for me on this to keep the sky blue while getting lighter on the trees, etc? ', '2005-02-28 18:29:08.000000', NULL, 0),
